1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 e6 3. d4 d5 { This is a uncommon opening } 4. exd5 exd5 5. dxc5 { I know this is the line here, but I dont know why I should capture those pawn } 5... Bxc5 6. Bd3 Be6 7. O-O Nf6 8. Bg5 Nbd7 9. Nc3 h6 10. Bh4 O-O 11. Qd2 Bb4 12. a3 Bxc3 13. Qxc3 Rc8 14. Qd2 Qc7 15. h3 { I play h3 to prevent the Ng4 } { [%csl Gg4][%cal Gf6g4] } 15... a6 16. Rfe1 Rfe8 17. Nd4 { my plan here is to capture that Bishop, But I realize that it will help my opponent to improve the position } { [%csl Ge6][%cal Gd4e6] } 17... Qb6 18. Nb3 Kh8 19. Kh1 { Kh1 to play f4 } 19... Qa7 20. f4 d4 21. Bf2 Bxb3 22. cxb3 Nd5 23. Bf5 { I found this move that stun Aldrin hahaha } 23... Rxe1+ 24. Rxe1 Rd8 { checkmate is incoming. When I play the Bf5 I already feel that there is a checkmate } 25. Bxd7 Rxd7 26. Re8+ Kh7 27. Qd3+ g6 28. Bxd4 Nxf4 29. Rh8# { Aldrin admit that he Didn't see the checkmate. he was shocked during our game } *


